0. Draft status and application

This is a proposed agreement, not an effective commercial license or a statement
that all relicensing rights have been confirmed. It must not be used for a
commercial release until ownership and third-party rights are confirmed, legal
review is complete, and the placeholders above are completed. The proposed
manifest reference identifies this draft only. This preparation branch does not
relicense previously published code or start a trial for its existing users.
Prior grants remain governed by their original terms; see section 8 and the
archived texts in docs/licensing/.

Once approved and effective, this agreement applies only to versions of Make It
Work expressly released by Licensor under this agreement (the Software). Public
availability of source code does not make those versions open-source licensed.
An individual accepting for an organization represents that they are authorized
to bind it. The organization accepting these terms is Customer. Licensor must
present these terms and obtain acceptance before installation or execution of a
commercially licensed version. A written order accepted by both parties (Order
Form) identifies Customer, fees, currency, payment due date, subscription start
and end dates, and any expressly included affiliates or additional terms.

1. Free trial

Customer may evaluate the Software for its internal business operations for one
30-day evaluation period per organization, beginning at its first installation
or execution of a commercially licensed version, whichever occurs first. The
trial includes use by Customer's employees and authorized contractors solely on
Customer's behalf, and internal modifications for that evaluation. Reinstalling,
upgrading, using a different developer account or machine, or removing trial
records does not restart or extend the trial. Use of an earlier version under a
prior license does not itself trigger this trial.

After 30 days, continued use of commercially licensed versions requires an
active paid annual subscription. Without one, Customer must stop using those
versions and remove operational copies, including internal modifications.
Customer may retain an inaccessible archival copy solely as required by law,
not for execution or further use. Customer's own artifacts and prior-license
rights are unaffected. The trial carries no payment obligation unless Customer
separately orders a subscription; it does not automatically convert to paid use.

2. Annual organization license

Subject to payment and compliance, Licensor grants Customer a nonexclusive,
nontransferable license for a 12-month subscription term to install, execute,
copy internally, and internally modify the Software for Customer's internal
business operations. Unlimited employees and authorized contractors may use it
solely on Customer's behalf, across unlimited internal repositories and
installations. Contractors receive no independent license and must be bound by
restrictions at least as protective as these terms; Customer is responsible for
their use. Internal access by these authorized users is permitted and is not
prohibited redistribution or sublicensing.

Customer means the single legal organization named in the Order Form. Parent
companies, subsidiaries, and other affiliates are excluded unless expressly
included in that Order Form. No seat-based or repository-based limit applies
within the licensed organization. Continued use after the 12-month term requires
renewal; the license is not perpetual, including for copies downloaded or
modified while subscribed. Customer may use and deliver its own work products,
including commercial products, as described in section 5.

3. Restrictions and public hosting

Except for authorized internal access above or express written permission from
Licensor, Customer must not redistribute, resell, sublicense, rent, lend, or
transfer the Software or its modifications, or offer the plugin itself as a
hosted commercial service. Customer must preserve applicable copyright, license,
and third-party notices and must not misrepresent ownership or remove notices
from internal copies. No trademark rights are granted.

These restrictions do not limit rights required by applicable law, rights under
prior licenses, or independent third-party licenses. They do not restrict
GitHub's or its users' rights to host, view, and fork the public repository
through GitHub functionality under applicable GitHub terms. Such hosting rights
do not independently grant a right to execute commercially licensed versions
outside these terms or to redistribute them outside those platform rights.

4. Fees, payment, and renewal

Fees, currency, taxes, payment method, and due dates are specified in the Order
Form; this agreement sets no price. Customer pays applicable transaction taxes
other than taxes on Licensor's income. Fees are nonrefundable except as expressly
agreed or required by law. Licensor may suspend the subscription for overdue,
undisputed payment after written notice and a 15-day opportunity to cure; any
termination for breach follows section 9.

Renewal requires a new Order Form or other written agreement; there is no
automatic renewal or charge unless separately and expressly agreed. Licensor
will disclose proposed renewal fees before Customer agrees to renew. A renewal
begins on the agreed date and lasts 12 months. A gap in subscription provides no
right to use commercially licensed versions during that gap. Expiration or
nonrenewal has the same cessation and removal obligations as trial expiration.

5. Intellectual property and Customer artifacts

As between the parties, InsideOut AI, through the legal Licensor identified
above, retains ownership of the Software and its intellectual property, only to
the extent it owns or is authorized to license those rights. Third-party rights
are reserved. This statement is subject to confirmation of ownership and is not
an assignment of contributor or third-party rights. Customer retains rights it
holds in its own internal modifications, subject to Licensor's rights in the
underlying Software and the use restrictions in this agreement. No ownership of
Customer modifications is automatically transferred to Licensor.

Customer retains ownership of its own code, requirements, documents, data, and
artifacts generated using Make It Work, to the extent those rights exist. No
ownership in those materials is transferred to Licensor. Customer may continue
to use, modify, distribute, and commercialize those materials after expiration
or termination without a Make It Work subscription. This does not grant rights
to distribute embedded copies of the Software, its proprietary templates or
other pre-existing materials, or third-party content. Ordinary generated work
products are not Software merely because Make It Work helped create them.
Licensor makes no promise that AI-generated output is unique, copyrightable,
accurate, or free of third-party claims.

6. Maintenance

An active annual subscription includes access to generally available updates,
improvements, bug fixes, and ongoing maintenance releases for the Software
during the subscription. Licensor does not commit to any particular release,
feature, fix, response time, resolution time, or support service-level agreement
unless separately agreed in writing. Updates remain subject to the applicable
commercial license; downloading them does not restart a trial or extend the
subscription. Access to new updates and maintenance ends on expiration.

7. Third-party components and services

Separately identified third-party components remain under their own licenses;
this agreement does not replace those licenses or restrict their independent
grants. Required notices must be preserved. Claude Code, AI providers, issue
trackers, and other external tools are supplied under their respective terms.
Customer obtains necessary accounts, permissions, and subscriptions and is
responsible for deciding what data to send to them and reviewing generated work.
Their fees are not included unless an Order Form says otherwise. Licensor does
not control their availability, processing practices, outputs, or changes.
This agreement does not authorize telemetry or collection of Customer content.

8. Previously published versions

Rights granted under previously published versions, including the PolyForm
Internal Use License 1.0.0 and the earlier MIT License, are expressly preserved
under those original terms. Previously published versions remain available in
repository history under their original licensing terms. This agreement neither
revokes nor narrows those grants, imposes a subscription on their exercise, nor
converts them to this license. It applies only to versions expressly released
under the new commercial agreement. Continued access to prior versions does not
include later commercial updates or maintenance. Prior-license terms govern any
breach or termination of prior-license rights, independently of this agreement.

9. Termination

Either party may terminate for the other's material breach if not cured within
30 days after written notice describing the breach. Customer may discontinue use
at any time; doing so does not excuse accrued payment obligations. Trial and
subscription rights also expire at their stated end without notice. Upon
expiration or termination, Customer must stop using the applicable commercially
licensed Software and remove operational copies and modifications, subject to
the legally required archival exception in section 1. Accrued payment duties,
ownership, restrictions, disclaimers, liability limits, dispute provisions, and
prior-license protections survive as relevant. Customer's own artifacts remain
Customer's property and may continue to be used under section 5.

10. Warranties and liability

TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, THE SOFTWARE, MAINTENANCE, AND UPDATES
ARE PROVIDED AS IS AND AS AVAILABLE, WITHOUT WARRANTIES, INCLUDING IMPLIED
WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, TITLE, AND
NONINFRINGEMENT. Customer is responsible for testing changes, reviewing output,
and maintaining appropriate backups.

TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, NEITHER PARTY IS LIABLE FOR INDIRECT,
INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, CONSEQUENTIAL, OR PUNITIVE DAMAGES, OR LOST PROFITS, REVENUE,
OR DATA ARISING UNDER THIS AGREEMENT. Each party's aggregate liability under
this agreement is limited to fees paid or payable under it for the 12 months
preceding the event giving rise to the claim. That cap does not excuse Customer's
payment obligations or limit liability for fraud, willful misconduct, or
infringement or misappropriation of the other party's intellectual property.
Neither the exclusions nor the cap limits liability that applicable law does
not permit the parties to exclude or limit. Mandatory statutory rights remain.

11. General terms

The laws of [GOVERNING JURISDICTION], excluding its conflict-of-laws rules,
govern this agreement; its competent courts have jurisdiction over disputes,
subject to mandatory law. Notices to Licensor go to [LICENSING CONTACT EMAIL]
and to Customer at its Order Form contact. Amendments require written agreement;
new website text alone does not change an existing subscription's terms. An
Order Form overrides this agreement only where it expressly identifies the
provision being varied. This agreement and applicable Order Form are the entire
agreement for the covered commercial versions, without superseding prior grants
or independent third-party terms. An unenforceable provision will be limited to
the extent necessary and the remaining provisions remain effective. Failure to
enforce a provision is not a waiver. Neither party may assign this agreement
without the other's written consent. No rights are granted by implication.
